resources.string:
Sometimes the MedLink confirms a bolus, start or stop but the pump does not apply it, usually because an alarm or message is open on the pump screen.

This number is used for:
• tries to connect to the MedLink;
• repetitions of a command sent to the MedLink (a command that reaches this many tries is given up);
• bolus tries (each try is checked with the pump history before sending again, so a bolus is never doubled);
• start and stop retries;
• how many such commands in a row show the warning "the pump probably shows an alarm on its screen".

Default 5. Lower values warn sooner but give up sooner.
